WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.310
Gaia the Dragon Champion attacks!

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.120
Flame Swordsman is destroyed!

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.630
I fuse Summoned Skull and Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.320
B. Skull Dragon, destroy Gaia the Dragon Champion!

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.080
Meteor Flare!

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.170
Yugi, I'm finally starting to understand the thrill of dueling.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.400
You're right.  This is a true duel, Jonouchi!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.310
The battle is only getting started!

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.740
Bring it on, Yugi!

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.380
Yeah!  Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:17.380
Finals of Friendship!
Yugi vs Jonouchi (Part 2)

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.820
This is a splendid duel.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:37.670
It's Yugi boy's technique vs Jonouchi boy's power.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:45.110
But Jonouchi boy has added tactics to his power, so he's pressuring Yugi boy.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.550
So Yugi boy, what will you do?

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.850
Next is Yugi's turn.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.560
There's no way Yugi will give up.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.680
This match is only getting started.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.890
But Jonouchi is just as determined.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.830
This duel will only get fiercer.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.650
What's the matter, Yugi?

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.020
Are you giving up?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.380
No.  I'll play this card this turn.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.800
Dark Magician in attack position!

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.900
Yugi is synonymous with Dark Magician.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.550
You finally played it.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.100
But it's no match for my B. Skull Dragon!

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.290
I know.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:40.320
Against a monster with greater attack points, it'll always defeat yours if they battle.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.360
Isn't that what you said before?

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:49.770
But Jonouchi, I also said that the combination of monster and spell cards form the foundation of dueling.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.440
You don't mean...

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.440
The spell card Magical Hats!

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.520
Magical Hats...

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.540
That's...

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.820
Yugi used that card before.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.260
You're using one of your special techniques, Yugi boy.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:16.000
Jonouchi, which hat is Dark Magician hiding under?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.920
I knew he would eventually play this, but it really is troublesome.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.140
Which Magical Hat is Dark Magician hiding under?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.680
Let's battle!

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.950
I have no choice but to crush them one at a time!

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.520
Go, B. Skull Dragon!

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.890
Did I succeed?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.330
You missed, Jonouchi.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.260
There are three hats left.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.700
Damn!  Which Magical Hat is Dark Magician hiding inside?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:58.060
Jonouchi seems to be spending more time thinking.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.810
That means he's really thinking about his strategies.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:04.360
He might try something this turn.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:09.060
Didn't you say you would destroy my monsters one at at time, Jonouchi?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.750
So what will you do now?

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.820
If I destroy Dark Magician, you have nothing left.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.510
So it would be a shame to end this duel against you so quickly.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.260
How's this?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.270
Garoozis in attack position!

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.620
What are you thinking?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:34.920
It has 1800 attack points, and Dark Magician has 2500 attack points.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.200
I'll let you win this turn.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:38.950
What?

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.320
I want to keep dueling you!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:47.540
I can easily destroy your Dark Magician right now, but that would be boring.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.960
So I'll let you have this.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.440
Go ahead and attack, Yugi.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.700
Has Jonouchi lost his mind?

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.640
No, he's trying to make Yugi attack.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:06.580
Jonouchi is trying to draw Dark Magician out of the Magical Hats.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.740
What's wrong?  Attack me!

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.010
It's your turn.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.450
Jonouchi, I'm not going to fall for that one.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.590
I hide this card under one of my Magical Hats and end my turn.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.880
What did he hide?

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.180
It's your turn, Jonouchi.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.900
I guess I can't trick you so easily.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.540
He plans to hide Dark Magician under his Magical Hats as long as he can.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:38.500
And he also hid something else.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.240
I bet it's a trap card.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.370
Jonouchi must think that I hid a trap card.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.950
But does he still have the courage to attack?

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.500
Damn, thinking isn't helping me.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.640
I'll just have to strike hard.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.160
B. Skull Dragon, battle!

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.100
Meteor Flare!

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.550
This is the perfect time to Mind Scan.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.980
I can clearly see them trying to figure out what the other is thinking.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.920
The next turn is the issue.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.320
Two Magical Hats remain.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.860
Depending on which hat he attacks, the course of this battle will change greatly.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.380
They're trying hard to read each other.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:39.640
I can't believe Jonouchi is trying to outwit Yugi.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:40.580
Yeah.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.840
That could have never happened before.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.680
But he's grown into a fantastic duelist.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.010
For some reason, I feel chills.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.250
There are two Magical Hats left.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:02.220
One contains Dark Magician, and the other contains my set card.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.630
That means you're going to hit something.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.000
You're right.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.430
Is the other card inside Magical Hats a trap card?

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.670
Attack and you'll find out.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.640
Fine.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:23.100
But no matter what happens, I won't run away because my opponent is no ordinary duelist!

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.150
Yugi, here I go!

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:29.250
B. Skull Dragon, attack Magical Hats!

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.760
Meteor Flare!

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.340
Spellbinding Circle!

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:57.200
Spellbinding Circle?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.180
It dropped its attack points!  This is bad.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.850
Just in case, I'll switch Garoozis to defense position.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.840
It's my turn, Jonouchi.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.800
It's not easy to defeat Yugi.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.230
But Jonouchi is doing really well.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:19.600
You're right.  His attack didn't succeed this turn, but they're on equal strengths now.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:24.000
Since they played all their strongest monsters...

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.780
...Yugi should the advantage because he has more helpful spells.  But...

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.600
But what?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:33.580
Dueling is complex because nothing goes according to theory.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.240
I knew you wouldn't let me win that easily.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.460
What should I do?

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.800
He's tough.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:46.200
Jonouchi no longer fears any opponent.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.640
And he's not reckless.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.400
He can calmly make decisions like a duelist.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:57.340
Jonouchi, you're an opponent worthy of my full power.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.300
This has turned into a battle of wills.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.580
I'm looking forward to seeing how this ends.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.200
But I can't just keep admiring him.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.250
There will come a time to end this.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:17.190
I will do whatever it takes to destroy B. Skull Dragon!

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.230
Yeah?  Go ahead and try!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.140
It's my turn.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:29.540
I hope you're ready, Jonouchi.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.730
Book of Secret Arts!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:04.600
This spell card raises Dark Magician's attack points by 300!

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:10.940
Battle!

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.350
Black Magic!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:24.040
B. Skull Dragon is destroyed!

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.230
Bravo, Yugi boy.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:34.130
Yugi, you're strong.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.260
You're really strong.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:39.140
I really can't defeat Yugi?

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:43.680
Jonouchi, this is proof of our friendship.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:48.620
No matter the outcome, we'll both give all our power.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:52.750
That's how we duel, right Jonouchi?

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:59.100
Jonouchi, you've done well, but there's no point going any further-

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.400
That's still too early to say.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.220
What do you mean?

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.970
In Yugi and Jonouchi's hearts, this duel isn't over yet.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:12.020
Their desire to duel each other hasn't ended yet.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:16.840
I managed to survive so far, but if nothing changes, I can't win.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.140
Damn!  What should I do?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:20.620
Big brother.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.650
Shizuka?

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:26.090
I wanted to see your face one last time.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.720
Promise?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.180
Yeah!  It's a promise!

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.600
That's right.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.800
You're waiting for me.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.110
That's right.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:47.610
No matter what happens, I can't afford to lose!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.670
What did he draw?

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:03.160
The real battle is only getting started, Yugi!

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:07.330
Baby Dragon in attack position!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.060
And I set this card.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.340
Is that set card Time Wizard?

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:26.000
If it is, he will transform Baby Dragon into Thousand Dragon and attack.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.700
I have to destroy it before then!

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:28.960
Battle!

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.320
Dark Magician, attack Baby Dragon!

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.520
Black Magic!

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.860
I don't think so!

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:40.280
I activate a trap card!

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.040
What?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.220
Garoozis, take Kunai with Chain!

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:59.410
Oh no!  Due to Baby Dragon, I mistakenly thought it would be Time Wizard.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:03.020
Yugi boy, you were momentarily perplexed.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:09.360
Since you know each other's strategies really well, you can be misled by a single card.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:14.640
That's what makes this duel both complex and entertaining.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.400
It's almost time to end things, Yugi.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.570
You're right, Jonouchi.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.640
Yugi.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.540
What?

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.980
No matter who wins, no hard feelings.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:35.750
I know.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:38.920
Yugi...  Jonouchi...

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.420
I've fought hard to get this far.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.460
Even I'm impressed with myself.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:48.480
But my battle isn't over yet.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.630
It's over when I finish you!

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.800
I'm betting everything on my next draw.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:15:00.080
Even if I lose this duel, I'll have no regrets.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.020
All right!

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.420
I drew the best card to decide our match!

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:10.950
What?  Can it be?

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:12.120
Here I go!

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:13.820
Time Wizard!

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.720
Time Wizard?

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:22.430
I never imagined that I'd use this card to determine our fate.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:25.630
Oh yeah.  Use this.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.400
It should help in an emergency.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.680
Okay.  Thanks!

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:39.380
It has gotten me out of quite a few pinches so far.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:44.160
Yugi, I wouldn't be dueling you right now if it wasn't for this card.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:50.110
Time Wizard will decide our fate, which is the most appropriate end for us!

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.880
Face my best card, Yugi!

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.830
Time Wizard, Time Roulette!

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.250
All right!  Success!

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.580
Time Magic!

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:27.640
Due to the passage of time, Dark Magician becomes old!

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.540
Dark Magician...

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.460
...is turning into a geezer!

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:35.030
Is Jonouchi going to win?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.660
I can't believe it.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.840
I'm finally going to beat Yugi.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.400
This isn't a dream or an illusion.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.480
Don't hate me, Yugi.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:54.980
I win!  Battle!

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.360
Thousand Nose Breath!

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:01.900
Makiu!

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:05.630
What?

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:09.740
Impossible!

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.770
What's going on?

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:14.240
How did Makiu activate during my turn?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:20.040
Jonouchi, your Baby Dragon isn't the only monster that Time Wizard can transform.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:20.810
What?

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.820
When a magician ages a millennium...

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:31.300
...he becomes a sage that possesses all wisdom!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.580
This is Dark Sage!

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:44.670
During each of our turns, Dark Sage allows me to add a spell card in my deck to my hand.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:49.710
I used that effect during your turn to get Makiu and make it rain.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:55.710
And on my turn, I can get another spell card.

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:03.840
Jonouchi, it's my turn.

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:12.640
Dark Sage's tremendous power lets me use a spell card!

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:14.500
Monster Reborn!

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:21.610
I revive B. Skull Dragon in attack position!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.120
Yugi.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:33.020
Bring it on, Yugi!

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.820
Battle!

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.360
They're both incredible.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:04.360
Yeah.  They're true duelists.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:11.920
I think I finally understand why two people with a strong bond would battle.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:16.000
That was wonderful.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.760
They showed me a fine duel.

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:23.680
Yugi boy, I promise to defeat you.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.380
Yugi, take it.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.060
This belongs to you.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.660
Jonouchi, you keep the prize money.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:54.970
My goal is to defeat Pegasus and save Grandpa and Kaiba.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:57.940
Use the prize money for Shizuka's operation.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.800
Yugi...

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:03.060
Would you do that for me?

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:04.990
Take it, Jonouchi.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:07.980
Now Shizuka's eyes will be healed.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.040
Thank you, Yugi.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:17.840
Make sure you defeat Pegasus.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:35.760
Yugi finally challenges Pegasus to a final battle.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:41.760
Pegasus's Millennium Eye lets him see his opponent's hand, but don't lose, Yugi!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.000
For Grandpa, Kaiba and Mokuba!

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.800
Huh?  Where's Honda?

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.420
Sheesh!  Where did he go at a time like this?

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Final Duel
Yugi vs Pegasus

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.280
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:11.050
The flask glistens

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:18.900
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:27.880
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:35.650
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:41.480
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:45.590
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:53.870
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:58.100
Shower of happiness

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.230
You are not alone

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:08.950
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
